# The abstract model — terminology, facets, the value axis, order, the graph, metadata,
# matching, and the constructs-in-concretes matrix; each a subdirectory chapter.
!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
The logical model
description: omnivorous nodes with ordered relations — the terminology and the type system
- |
  Beneath every surface and every storage form there is one logical model: a graph of
  **omnivorous nodes** connected by **ordered relations**. A node may carry a scalar value
  of its own, named entries, and positional entries — all at once; the relations between
  nodes keep their order as data. This part defines the model precisely: the terms, the
  three facets a node exercises, the value types, where order lives, the graph shape, the
  metadata layer, and how consumers match against it all.
- *: terminology
- *: facets
- *: values
- *: order
- *: graph
- *: metadata
- *: matching
- *: constructs
